# Compiled operator binary. `make` writes it here (k8s-operator/Makefile:
# BINARY_NAME ?= bin/manager), so it is build output, not source. A 30 MB
# developer build was committed once and it was a macOS arm64 executable -- it
# could not even run on the Linux cluster it was supposedly for. This repository
# is public, so a committed binary is also unverifiable provenance and carries
# whatever strings were baked in at build time.
k8s-operator/bin/
